memo-rag (0.14.3-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Databases sharing an index directory keep separate index files: each
    PostgreSQL namespace without its own index_dir used the same file in
    /var/lib/memo/indices. Files are now named after the database's name
    and id, and an existing file is adopted by the database it belongs
    to, so upgrading doesn't rebuild it.

 -- trans <trans@github.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

memo-rag (0.14.2-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * memo-arcana takes its namespaces from /etc/memo/namespaces.yaml; an
    open request registers others only with MEMO_BUS_OPEN=1. List every
    namespace a client opens over the bus in namespaces.yaml.
  * A namespace opened over the bus never gets the server's API key, and
    open can't redirect a registered namespace to another database.
  * A search's limit is capped at 1000 (a huge one allocated gigabytes).
  * Database passwords are redacted in the startup log and error replies.
  * Chunking is linear for non-ASCII text, and no chunk exceeds the
    token limit; indexing a new source id concurrently doesn't fail.

 -- trans <trans@github.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

memo-rag (0.14.1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Search filters apply to every result: sources that share a text with
    a matching one no longer come back when the filters exclude them.
  * An id filter that names no source finds nothing, instead of being
    dropped; search raises for filters it can't apply.
  * An older text no longer overwrites a newer one indexed during its
    embedding; deleting a source cancels its queued work; a blank text
    removes the source's old chunks.

